  "transfer_invariants": [
    "A physical unit or owned lot keeps canonical ID, variant, species family and physical size across pickup, carrying, belt, dock, stock and counter.",
    "No context-specific shrink-to-fit, scale interpolation to a different end size, random reroll of variant or species substitution at a handoff.",
    "Larger piles use more visible units or honest representative grouping under existing quantities; they do not enlarge one ordinary unit.",
    "Existing generic meat/fish stays generic or unknown; never invent species provenance for old saved stock.",
    "Processing changes canonical ID only through an existing authored recipe. fish\u2192cooked_fish and meat\u2192meal retain the known source species family in output presentation.",
    "A processed output has its own selected appearance/bounds; after creation those bounds remain unchanged through its transfers. This does not require raw and cooked geometry to be identical.",
    "If a permitted batch combines different source variants, keep per-source presentation provenance or show a neutral mixed output; never falsely reclassify the whole batch as one species.",
    "Typed ports accept existing resource families/catalogue rules. Physical route fit must accommodate its largest accepted variant before release.",
    "Unsupported variants wait/reject recoverably; do not resize the item or chosen R1 conveyor secretly."
  ],
